---
import AcademicLayout from "../../layouts/AcademicLayout.astro";
---

<AcademicLayout title="Accessibility Statement" currentSection="about">
  <div class="container container-prose page-wrapper">
    <header class="page-header">
      <h1 class="page-title">Accessibility Statement</h1>
      <p class="page-lead">
        Symnoesis is committed to digital accessibility in compliance with WCAG 2.1 and 2.2 Level AA.
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="prose-content">
      <section>
        <h2>Accessible Design Standards</h2>
        <p>
          Scientific instruments and research literature must be fully legible to every researcher. 
          We have implemented the following accessibility features across the web application:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Keyboard Navigation:</strong> The 16×16 interactive map supports full keyboard operation using a roving tabindex, standard arrow-key navigation, and wrap-around movement.</li>
          <li><strong>Accessible Table Alternative:</strong> The map includes a complete sortable and navigable table alternative rendering all 256 states with explicit labels for screen readers.</li>
          <li><strong>Color Vision Deficiency Support:</strong> The diverging SQ palette is mapped in OKLab color space and tested for protanopia, deuteranopia, and tritanopia. Color is never the sole indicator of sign or state: glyphs (+/−) and textual zone labels accompany all cells.</li>
          <li><strong>High Contrast & Semantic Landmarks:</strong> Body copy meets or exceeds a 4.5:1 contrast ratio against the background. Skip links allow immediate bypass of navigation headers.</li>
          <li><strong>Motion Sensitivity:</strong> All animations honor <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> settings. Autoplay is disabled everywhere.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Known Limitations & Feedback</h2>
        <p>
          We continually audit this site against automated accessibility suites and screen reader devices. 
          If you encounter any barrier, please file an issue on our GitHub repository.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</AcademicLayout>

<style>
  .page-wrapper { padding: 3rem 0; }
  .page-header { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 2rem; }
  .page-title { font-size: var(--text-h1); font-weight: 700; margin: 0.75rem 0 1rem 0; color: var(--ink); }
  .page-lead { font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--ink-2); line-height: 1.5; margin: 0; }
  .prose-content { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: var(--text-body); line-height: 1.7; color: var(--ink); }
  .prose-content h2 { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: var(--text-h2); font-weight: 600; margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem 0; color: var(--ink); }
  .prose-content p { margin: 0 0 1.25rem 0; }
  .prose-content ul { margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0; padding-left: 1.5rem; }
  .prose-content li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
</style>
